Subject: [PATCH] cmake/python: honor a pre-pinned wheel version

Base: upstream linphone-sdk commit 7d5fe98a18ff7be2381656b600f880e3c49f5089
      (master, 2025-12-23), vendored under third_party/linphone-sdk/.

This patch is applied automatically by poc-linphone/scripts/build_linphone_sdk.sh
before configuring the SDK build, and reverted after the build completes. The
linphone-sdk source tree is otherwise untouched.

Why this patch exists
=====================

When the linphone-sdk source is vendored under poc-linphone/third_party/
(via `git subtree`), `git describe` invoked inside that tree returns a tag
from the surrounding poc-linphone repository (e.g.
"proposed-attack-complete-25-g000ca4f367"), not from the upstream
linphone-sdk repository. Two places in the upstream cmake configure call
`git describe` and FATAL_ERROR if the output does not match a
major.minor.patch grammar:

  * bctoolbox/cmake/BCToolboxCMakeUtils.cmake — bc_compute_full_version()
    Already gated by `if(NOT LINPHONESDK_VERSION)` in the top-level
    CMakeLists.txt, so passing -DLINPHONESDK_VERSION=… on the cmake
    command line bypasses it.

  * cmake/python/GenerateWheel.cmake — bc_compute_python_wheel_version()
    Has no such gate. This patch adds one. When the caller sets
    -DWHEEL_LINPHONESDK_VERSION_PINNED=<version>, the function uses
    that value verbatim and skips the git describe probe.

In stock builds (where neither the gate variable is set), the function
behaves exactly as upstream.

---
 cmake/python/GenerateWheel.cmake | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cmake/python/GenerateWheel.cmake b/cmake/python/GenerateWheel.cmake
index 3cbe397ee1..6d919b5684 100644
--- a/cmake/python/GenerateWheel.cmake
+++ b/cmake/python/GenerateWheel.cmake
@@ -32,6 +32,13 @@ linphone_sdk_check_python_module_is_installed(wheel)

 # See https://packaging.python.org/guides/distributing-packages-using-setuptools/#id61
 function(bc_compute_python_wheel_version OUTPUT_VERSION)
+if(WHEEL_LINPHONESDK_VERSION_PINNED)
+    # PoC patch: honor caller-provided version; skip the git describe
+    # probe that fails when this tree is embedded in another git
+    # repository (e.g. as a vendored subtree under third_party/).
+    set(${OUTPUT_VERSION} "${WHEEL_LINPHONESDK_VERSION_PINNED}" CACHE STRING "" FORCE)
+    return()
+endif()
 find_program(GIT_EXECUTABLE git NAMES Git CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_BOTH)
 if(GIT_EXECUTABLE)
     execute_process(
